# Build options for rslidar_sdk in a colcon workspace.
#
# ENABLE_IMU_DATA_PARSE defaults to OFF upstream, and that default is a trap on a lidar
# that HAS an IMU. The Airy streams IMU on its own UDP port (51-byte packets at ~200 Hz on
# :6688 alongside MSOP on :6699) and decoder_RSAIRY.hpp implements decodeImuPkt - but the
# publisher lives behind `#ifdef ENABLE_IMU_DATA_PARSE`, so with the default the topic is
# not merely empty, it does not exist. Setting ros_send_imu_data_topic in the YAML looks
# like it should be enough and is not: the key is read inside the same ifdef.
#
# That matters because RKO-LIO is lidar-INERTIAL odometry. Without this flag mapping and
# localization have no IMU to fuse.
# POINT_TYPE is not listed here: this fork DEFAULTS to XYZIRT (ring + per-point
# timestamp), because every lidar it is used with feeds lidar-inertial odometry. Setting
# it again here would just be a second place to keep in step.
cmake-args:
  - -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  - -DENABLE_IMU_DATA_PARSE=ON
